program Four plus four.
note The kernel decides what is formal; a model is asked only what is not. Run it with any applicator: the fingerprint is the same.

let a = 4 + 4.
assert a = 8.
let exact = 0.1 + 0.2.
assert exact = 0.3 because "exact rational arithmetic, never floating point".
let third = 1 / 3.
assert third * 3 = 1.

ask legs: Int in 0..20 "How many legs does a spider have?" with effort=low
ensure legs = a else retry because "a spider has eight legs".
show [a, legs] as "kernel and model agree".
